{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>תחולל</b> — joined to the verse before and after; it is from חלילה, meaning תמנע. Another interpretation: from חולל אילות, like תכאבו באבנים, ראתה ותחל הארץ, יחיל ה' מדבר קדש — meaning it causes trembling. Likewise the interpretation of 'a north wind brings rain': it overpowers it until it is withheld and does not fall on the earth, for it scatters the clouds to the sides. And so an angry face will make a hidden tongue tremble — that through speaking of gossip in secret, the face given to it [shows] anger, until it restrains it from gossip. And this is a moral lesson: that one should not accept an evil tongue."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Resolved a possible copyist assimilation: the lemma should be תחולל (Prov. 25:23) but the MS reads תחלל; translated as the lemma form. Also note the third example citation is a conflation of Isaiah 35:2 (יחיל) and Psalm 29:8 (יחיל ה' מדבר קדש)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:45.876944003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}